    description: "When a .hypergumbo.toml holds a setting this hypergumbo does not know, the error says only \"unknown setting '<key>'. Known settings: ...\" (user_config.py:422). The likeliest cause when a repository adopts a new key is an older hypergumbo, and the message does not say so.\n\nOWNER RULING 2026-11-19 (in session, adopting the 11-19 review): an unknown project-tier key STAYS AN ERROR (fail closed: a later key may be a withholding gate, and a warning would let an older version silently skip it; user_config.py's docstring and ADR-0045 ruling 2 give the same reason). The message names the likely cause, e.g. \"this file may need a newer hypergumbo (this is <version>)\".\n\nSCOPE. The message only; tests in test_user_config.py / test_arbitration.py that match the text. Not in scope: ADR-0045 open question 4 (how the file declares its schema version), still not ruled, noted on WI-dahoh."  # 7cfe
    fields: {}  # 7cfe
